@startuml pkm-des-enrollment-sequence
autonumber
actor "Authenticated Student" as Student
participant "Browser" as Browser
participant "Server Action" as Action
participant "Domain Logic" as Logic
participant "Supabase Client" as Supabase
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

Student -> Browser : Clicks "Submit Enrollment"
Browser -> Action : submitEnrollmentAction()
Action -> Supabase : Get current Session & Profile
Supabase --> Action : Student ID
Action -> Supabase : Query trusted student, program, year, and type
Supabase --> Action : Student details (Year Level, Program, Type)

Action -> Logic : evaluateStandardLoadEligibility(context)
note right of Logic: Uses the active enrollment term
and the configured standard-load result.
Logic --> Action : "eligible"

Action -> Supabase : RPC submit_standard_student_enrollment(term)
note right of Supabase: The server supplies the term;\nthe database derives identity and load.

Supabase -> DB : Executes atomic RPC
DB -> DB : Checks unique student-term index (Duplicate protection)
DB -> DB : Resolves ACTIVE standard_load_sets and matching course_offerings
DB -> DB : Inserts PENDING enrollment
DB -> DB : Inserts offering-backed enrollment_subjects with snapshots
DB --> Supabase : Success
Supabase --> Action : Enrollment ID

note right of DB
  Client-provided active load: AY 2025-2026 / 2nd Semester
  workbook offerings are display reference data.
  They do not become the current load without
  an approved standard-load configuration.
end note

Action --> Browser : Redirect to Enrollment Status Page

@enduml
